>Bush robot? 

I expect this refers to the "fractal bush" robot or robot arm described by
Hans Moravec in _Mind Children_:  the end of each digit has two smaller
digits, down to the nanoscale.

>For instance, even though the average environmentalist seems
>to be a real power grabber, we don't have the technology to
>breathe poison safely yet, and it probably *is* stupid to
>flush toilets with drinking water.

Why do you think environmentalists are power grabbers?
Perhaps politicians become involved in environmental issues to gain
political power, at least in Germany, but the average environmentalist
is not seeking power in general -- certainly no more than any of us are
to advance our viewpoints.

I'm disturbed by the impression that people on this list
think environmentalists are nuts, and the Earth is in no danger.
(Well of course the Earth as a ball of nickel and rock is not in
danger, but the things on it...)  Have you all been reading
Rush Limbaugh?  Can we have an opinion poll, to see what the Extropian
viewpoint on this issue is?

Questions: Answer yes or no.

1.  Natural ecosystems and other natural life forms (e.g., not cows)
are good things worth preserving, even if there is no material benefit
and significant material loss to us from doing so.

2.  Natural ecosystems are being disrupted, species eradicated, and
the environment polluted at rates beyond optimal.

3.  There is a danger that if we do not reduce such disruption,
eradication, and pollution soon, it will be "too late" (feel free
to give your own interpretation of "too late").

4.  The Earth will soon have too many humans.

5.  The Earth has too many humans already.

6.  Population should increase until the Earth contains as many humans
as it can support.

7.  Everyone should be content to live in a city.  Country living is a
luxury which takes too many resources per individual.

8.  The Earth is ours, and we have no obligations to other species.

9.  Intellect is the greatest virtue, and creatures with greater intellect
should eventually replace all creatures of lesser intellect.


